  "body": "Allow activation of a checked radio button to clear it\n\nChange radio button activation so that activating the checked radio button again returns an optional radio group to its no-selection state.\n\nThis addresses optional questions in forms. For example, Chromium issue 40761596 describes an optional gender question whose instructions say not to select an option if none applies. Once a user accidentally selects a radio button, native radio behavior does not provide a way to return to the original no-selection state. The user must instead rely on the page providing a separate clear or reset control, use script, or discard the form.\n\nRadio groups already support a no-selection state: a group can initially have no checked radio button, and script can set a radio button's checkedness to false. This change makes that state reachable through user activation as well.\n\nTo preserve author-provided defaults, activating the checked radio button restores the group's checked content attribute default, if one exists, instead of clearing the group. For example, if the markup gives one radio button a `checked` attribute as a safe default, activating the currently checked radio button again returns the group to that default state.\n\nDemo: https://static.januschka.com/i-40761596/index.html\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium: interest not yet confirmed; tracking issue: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40761596\n   * Mozilla: position requested at https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1452\n   * WebKit: position requested at https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/721\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * Not yet submitted\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40761596\n   * Gecko: not yet filed\n   * WebKit: not yet filed\n   * Deno: not applicable\n   * Node.js: not applicable\n- [ ] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs:\n   * Not yet filed\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: not yet filed\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n\n### :boom: Error: write ECONNRESET :boom: ###\n\n[PR Preview](https://github.com/specinfra/pr-preview#pr-preview) failed to build. _(Last tried on Sep 8, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC)_.\n\n<details>\n<summary>More</summary>\n\n\nPR Preview relies on a number of web services to run. There seems to be an issue with the following one:\n\n:rotating_light: [Wattsi Server](https://github.com/domenic/wattsi-server) - Wattsi Server is the web service used to build the WHATWG HTML spec.\n\n:link: [Related URL](https://build.whatwg.org/wattsi)\n\n**Error output:**\n\n```\nNetwork error while accessing Wattsi server\n```\n\n_This seems to be an issue with the [Wattsi Server](https://github.com/domenic/wattsi-server) service. PR Preview doesn't manage this service and so has no control over it. If you've identified an issue with it, you can [report the issue to the maintainers of Wattsi Server](https://github.com/domenic/wattsi-server/issues/new) directly. Please be courteous. Thank you!_\n\n_If you don't have enough information above to solve the error by yourself or if the issue doesn't seem related to Wattsi Server, you can [file an issue with PR Preview](https://github.com/specinfra/pr-preview/issues/new?title=Unidentified%20Error&body=See%20whatwg/html%2312480.)._\n\n</details>\n\n",
